# T-002 Spike A: Avalonia + AvaloniaEdit

Status: queued
Owner: Codex Director `spike-a-director` (gpt-6.1-sol medium). Spawn Luna workers (`gpt-6-luna`, high) for implementation chunks; you integrate and verify.
Writable: `spikes/A/`, `docs/spikes/A/`, `.coord/` (STATUS.md checkpoints, report). Nothing else.
Report: `.coord/reports/T-002.md` plus `docs/spikes/A/REPORT.md`.
Work all milestones in ONE turn; checkpoint STATUS.md as you go; end the turn only when the report is written or you are blocked.

## Read first
AGENTS.md, docs/spike-spec.md, `.coord/reports/T-001.md`, docs/research/third-party.md (Avalonia section). Candidate packages: Avalonia 12.1.4, Avalonia.AvaloniaEdit + AvaloniaEdit.TextMate 12.0.0 (verify they restore; pin versions). .NET SDK 10.0.402 is installed.

## Order of work (stop early and report if a gate fails)
1. Gate 1, input probe FIRST: minimal Avalonia window logging pointer/wheel/gesture events with phases while the editor is focused. Distinguish contact movement, paused fingers, finger lift, inertia, cancel on a precision touchpad. Ask the user to do the two-finger pan when ready (write exact instructions in STATUS.md "Waiting on user"). If native events lack a finger-lift signal, try ONE bounded native adapter (e.g. Win32 pointer/Direct Manipulation) and report its scope.
2. Then the rest of docs/spike-spec.md: carousel (direct manipulation, release by distance+velocity, spring-back, rubber-band overscroll creating a new note, blank-note pruning), tray + global hotkey toggle of a resident frameless window, transparent/Acrylic/Mica, decorated markdown with visible markers, clickable `- [ ]` (undo/caret stable), Tab/Shift+Tab indent, fenced python highlight, autosave/restore, folding + line numbers probes, measurements (cold launch to editable, hotkey to visible+focused, hide time, idle RAM; scripted where possible).
3. About 10-15 smoke checks, disposable, header `# spike`. No exhaustive suites.

## Rules
- Local git only; commit your work in `spikes/A` and `docs/spikes/A` when done. Do not touch spikes/B.
- Do not install system software. If something is missing, record it as a blocker.
- REPORT.md: pass/fail per spec item, numbers, screenshots (save under docs/spikes/A/), effort estimate, blockers, and a plain-language verdict: would you build the real app on this?
